  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.5.1.4\"\n  python_min: \"3.11\"\n\npackage:\n  name: spacr\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/s/spacr/spacr-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 32113621263f931862d5ab63fb507819d2172276edb3bfdf42210bf3e7eea7bb\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . --no-deps --no-build-isolation -vv\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - spacr = spacr.qt:run\n      - spacr-qt = spacr.qt:run\n      - spacr-nightly = spacr.qt:run\n      - spaceout = spacr.qt.spaceout:main\n      - safespacr = spacr.qt.safespacr:main\n      - spacr-server = spacr.qt:run_without_setup\n      - spacr-tutorial = spacr.qt.tutorial.__main__:main\n      - spacr-repro = spacr.cli_repro:main\n      - spacr-workspace = spacr.cli_workspace:main\n      - spacr-make-masks = spacr.cli_make_masks:main\n      - spacr-run = spacr.cli:main\n      - spacr-download = spacr.cli_download:main\n      - spacr-remote = spacr.cli_remote:main\n      - spacr-plugins = spacr.cli_plugins:main\n      - spacr-leakage = spacr.cli_leakage:main\n      - spacr-db-audit = spacr.cli_database:main\n      - spacr-doctor = spacr.doctor:main\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=77\n    - wheel\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }},<3.15,!=3.14.1\n    - packaging >=21.3\n    - cloudpickle >=3.1.2,<4\n    - czifile\n    - numpy >=1.26.4,<3.0\n    - pandas >=2.2.1,<4.0\n    - scipy >=1.12.0,<2.0\n    - cellpose >=4.0.7,<5.0\n    # cellpose 4.1.1 imports this at runtime but its current conda-forge\n    # package omits the dependency.\n    - segment-anything >=1.0,<2.0\n    - scikit-image >=0.22.0,<0.28\n    - pywavelets >=1.4,<2\n    - scikit-learn >=1.5.0,<2.0\n    - scikit-posthocs >=0.10.0,<0.20\n    - trackpy >=0.6.2,<1.0\n    - statsmodels >=0.14.0,<0.15\n    - patsy >=0.5.6,<2.0\n    - shap >=0.47.0,<1.0\n    - pytorch >=2.0,<3.0\n    - pyfixest >=0.40.1,<1\n    - glum >=3.1.2,<4\n    - gpytorch >=1.11,<2\n    - tensorboard >=2.21,<3.0\n    - numba >=0.60,<1.0\n    - llvmlite >=0.43,<1.0\n    - torchvision >=0.15,<1.0\n    - captum >=0.7.0,<1.0\n    - seaborn >=0.13.2,<1.0\n    - matplotlib-base >=3.8.3,<4.0\n    - matplotlib-venn >=1.1,<2.0\n    - pypdf >=6.16.1,<7.0\n    - cycler >=0.10,<1\n    - pyqtgraph >=0.13.3,<1\n    - mpmath >=1.3,<2\n    - vispy >=0.14,<1.0\n    - adjusttext >=1.2.0,<2.0\n    - bottleneck >=1.3.6,<2.0\n    - numexpr >=2.8.4,<3.0\n    - opencv >=4.9.0,<5.0\n    - pillow >=10.2.0,<13\n    - tifffile >=2023.4.12\n    - nd2reader >=3.3.0,<4.0\n    - readlif\n    - openpyxl >=3.1,<4.0\n    - imageio >=2.34.0,<3.0\n    - umap-learn >=0.5.11,<1.0\n    - xgboost >=2.0.3,<4\n    - biopython >=1.80,<2.0\n    - lxml >=5.1.0\n    - psutil >=5.9.8,<8\n    - gputil >=1.4.0,<2.0\n    - nvidia-ml-py >=11.450.51,<14\n    - pytables >=3.8.0,<4.0\n    - screeninfo >=0.8.1,<1.0\n    - fastremap >=1.14.1\n    - tqdm >=4.65.0\n    - requests >=2.28,<3.0\n    - joblib >=1.2,<2.0\n    - natsort >=8.0,<9.0\n    - sympy >=1.12,<2.0\n    - ipython >=8.18.1,<10\n    - ipywidgets >=8.1.2,<9.0\n    - huggingface_hub >=0.25,<1.0\n    - protobuf >=5.28.3\n    # The conda package exposes the desktop entry point, so its GUI runtime\n    # must be explicit rather than relying on cellpose to pull a Qt binding.\n    - pyside6 >=6.6,<7\n    - qtawesome >=1.3,<2\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - spacr\n      # conda-forge's segment-anything package provides the importable module\n      # without PyPI dist-info, so pip check reports a false missing dependency.\n      # The script test below imports segment_anything and the spaCR GUI directly.\n      pip_check: false\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}\n        - \"*\"\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    script:\n      - python -c \"import cellpose, segment_anything, torch; from spacr import measure; from spacr.qt import run; assert callable(run)\"\n      - python -c \"import shutil; names = ('spacr', 'spacr-qt', 'spacr-nightly', 'spaceout', 'safespacr', 'spacr-server', 'spacr-tutorial', 'spacr-repro', 'spacr-workspace', 'spacr-make-masks', 'spacr-run', 'spacr-download', 'spacr-remote', 'spacr-plugins', 'spacr-leakage', 'spacr-db-audit', 'spacr-doctor'); assert all(shutil.which(name) for name in names)\"\n      - spacr-run --list\n\nabout:\n  summary: Spatial phenotype analysis of CRISPR screens\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  homepage: https://github.com/EinarOlafsson/spacr\n  repository: https://github.com/EinarOlafsson/spacr\n  documentation: https://einarolafsson.github.io/spacr/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - EinarOlafsson\n",
